{
  "id": "s1",
  "wireframe": "s1",
  "title": "Tutorial",
  "background": "room-light",
  "note": "The tutorial room. On the first launch the invite (the language is chosen only in Settings, s5); in the room, the current lesson at the top and the lesson list at the right, over the MVP round HUD of s7 without the timer, the anger meter, the roster and the role (Hud). After lesson 9 the game returns to the ship (the player's own, no session) with no end screen, where the game boots (the engineer, 2026-10-21). The nine lessons are the game's (GDD §15: Throwing replaced Delivery in #901); which lessons the MVP adds (points and the workbench, the neighbours' anger and the cops, a task) is open, the engineer's design. Lesson 2 names the battery, an MVP item (a draft; which item lies in the room is the game's data).",
  "states": [
    { "id": "invite", "label": "Запрошення", "note": "First launch only (a user:// flag). A quiet tile over the dimmed room; Start the tutorial takes focus with its ring hidden (below), so no control shows focus here." },
    { "id": "step", "label": "Крок навчання", "note": "Lesson 2, its first instruction: a sentence with one keycap." },
    { "id": "step-keys", "label": "Крок: керування", "note": "Lesson 1 (Controls): a row of keycaps instead of the sentence." },
    { "id": "step-howto", "label": "Крок: «?» на мапі", "note": "Lesson 5, its second instruction: the round «?» keycap inside the sentence. The map (s8) is open in this lesson; it is not drawn here, nor the HUD under its dim." },
    { "id": "step-dead", "label": "Крок: смерть", "note": "Lesson 7 (Death): the player died and waits in the dead's room (m8 §3), so the round HUD is hidden; the dead's room overlay is s9's and is not drawn here. Its two lines are drafts." }
  ],
  "nodes": [
